.TH DOWNTIME_LOGGER 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-downtime-logger 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
downtime_logger \- plugin interfaces of the Mu2e DAQ downtime logger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B from downtime_logger.detectors.base import Detector
.B from downtime_logger.core.event import DetectorState, DetectorReading, DowntimeEvent
.B from downtime_logger.core.metric import Metric
.B from downtime_logger.storage.base import StorageBackend
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B downtime_logger
package (installed by
.IR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger )
loads its detectors, its metric and its storage backend from YAML strings of
the form
.IR module.path:ClassName ,
using
.B importlib
(no entry points).
A class in any module on
.B PYTHONPATH
can be named.
Each is constructed with the YAML
.B options
mapping as keyword arguments.
.SS DetectorState
.B str
enum with values
.BR up ,
.B down
and
.BR unknown .
.SS Detector
A
.B QObject
with the signal
.BR "state_changed(str detector_id, str state, str detail)" .
.TP
.BI __init__( detector_id ", **options)"
Called on the GUI thread.
Call
.BI super().__init__( detector_id )\fR.
Accept and ignore unknown keywords with
.BR **_ ,
as the shipped detectors do.
Do not create sockets, timers or notifiers here: the object is moved to its
own
.B QThread
afterwards and anything created now keeps GUI\-thread affinity.
.TP
.B start()
A
.BR @Slot() .
Invoked once on the detector's thread through a queued
.BR QMetaObject.invokeMethod .
Create all I/O objects here.
An exception escaping
.B start()
is printed by PySide6 and swallowed; the detector then stays UNKNOWN with no
other indication.
.TP
.B stop()
A
.BR @Slot() ,
default no\-op.
Connected with a direct connection to the thread's
.B finished
signal, so it runs on the detector thread during shutdown.
.TP
.BI _emit_state( state ", " detail )
Emit
.BR state_changed ;
repeated identical states are suppressed after the first emission, so emit
on every observation and let the base class edge\-detect.
Report UNKNOWN when nothing can be determined; UNKNOWN is excluded from the
score.
.PP
The
.B weight
key in YAML is not passed to the detector.
.SS Metric
Abstract base class with one method:
.PP
.RS
.nf
evaluate(readings: Mapping[str, DetectorReading],
         previously_down: bool) \-> tuple[float, bool]
.fi
.RE
.PP
It returns the score (stored as given) and whether the state machine should
consider the DAQ down.
.I previously_down
lets the metric implement hysteresis.
The
.B debounce_seconds
option is removed from the metric options and consumed by the state
machine.
The shipped
.B WeightedRatioMetric(trip_threshold=0.6, clear_threshold=0.2)
returns
.IR sum(w_down)/sum(w_up+w_down) ,
0.0 when every detector is UNKNOWN.
.SS StorageBackend
Abstract base class; every method is called on the Qt GUI thread, and the
read methods are also called concurrently from HTTP request threads.
.TP
.BI open_event( event ") \-> int"
Persist a new event, set
.B event.id
in place and return it.
.TP
.BI close_event( event )
Persist
.BR ended_at .
.TP
.BI update_event( event )
Persist the editable fields.
The SQLite backend writes
.BR category ,
.BR subsystem ,
.BR cause ,
.B notes
and
.BR ended_at ;
it does not write
.BR started_at .
.TP
.BI get_event( id "), delete_event(" id ") \-> bool"
Fetch; hard delete.
.TP
.BI list_events( limit "=200)"
Newest first by
.BR started_at .
.TP
.BI list_events_in_range( start ", " end ", " limit "=5000)"
Events overlapping
.RI [ start ", " end ],
oldest first; events with no
.B ended_at
always overlap.
Pass UTC: the SQLite backend compares offset\-less UTC strings.
.TP
.BI log_readings( score ", " readings )
Append the readings of one recompute.
.TP
.B close()
Release resources.
.PP
The SQLite backend returns naive
.B datetime
objects that hold UTC wall\-clock time.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHONPATH
Where third\-party plugin modules are found.
.SH EXAMPLES
A detector that reports DOWN while a file exists:
.PP
.RS
.nf
import os
from PySide6.QtCore import QTimer, Slot
from downtime_logger.core.event import DetectorState
from downtime_logger.detectors.base import Detector

class FlagFileDetector(Detector):
    def __init__(self, detector_id, path, poll_s=2.0, **_):
        super().__init__(detector_id)
        self._path, self._ms, self._t = path, int(poll_s * 1000), None

    @Slot()
    def start(self):
        self._t = QTimer()
        self._t.timeout.connect(self._poll)
        self._t.start(self._ms)

    @Slot()
    def stop(self):
        if self._t:
            self._t.stop()

    def _poll(self):
        down = os.path.exists(self._path)
        self._emit_state(DetectorState.DOWN if down else DetectorState.UP,
                         self._path)
.fi
.RE
.PP
Referenced from YAML as
.BR "plugin: flagfile:FlagFileDetector" .
